; Chapter 3 §3.1: a library with terms lying around at the top level, to show
; what a library file CANNOT contribute to a program.
;
;   go run ./cmd/oro -target=tutorial docs/book/code/noisy-prog.oro
;
; `(+ 1 2)` and `(* 9 9)` below are reduced by nobody and printed by nobody:
; bare top-level terms in a LIBRARY are discarded (modules.md §5). And this
; file's `(export k)` is visibility only — it is not the program's entry point.

(module noisy-lib)

(export k)

(def k (n) (* n 3))

(+ 1 2)
(* 9 9)
